  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Given ADR-050 (concise, and the full version if one exists), when read, then the preset list is ConfirmModal, ChoiceModal, FormModal, PreviewModal, BrowseModal, WizardShell; WizardModal is recorded as retired; an "Amended 2026-10-07 (D-26)" marker is present.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given ADR-050, when read, then it contains the MUSTs on WizardShell as the only wizard engine, the in-app launch rule, embedded hideTitle under platform chrome, dismiss explicit + uiScale for wizards, and the MUST NOT on injecting CSS/DOM into platform chrome.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Given MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md, record-modal-selection.md and modal-shell.md, when read, then none says WizardShell comes from @spaarke/legal-workspace, none tells yes/no confirms to use a raw Fluent Dialog, and none says to compose RecordNavigationModalShell.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Negative: the Layout 1 OOB dialog rules, fullCover escalation and per-entity-size MUST NOT are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">A .claude/CHANGELOG.md entry names D-26 and this task.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
AMENDMENT TEXT FOR THE MAIN SESSION (from notes/modal-wizard-canonical-approach.md section 6; owner-adopted D-26, 2026-10-07). Apply to ADR-050:

1. Decision: the preset list becomes ConfirmModal, ChoiceModal, FormModal, PreviewModal, BrowseModal, WizardShell. WizardShell is the engine-bearing wizard preset: it renders inside SprkModal, and its embedded mode (no envelope) is the sanctioned variant for workspace tabs, full pages and pages hosted under platform chrome. WizardModal is retired (it had zero consumers).
2. MUST: every multi-step flow uses WizardShell. No other wizard engine or reducer may be introduced.
3. MUST (launch rule): when the caller is a Spaarke React surface (Console/SpaarkeAi widgets, LegalWorkspace sections running in SpaarkeAi, code pages, PCFs with the component in their bundle), open modals and wizards in-app via the SprkModal family. Xrm.Navigation.navigateTo(webresource|custom, {target:2}) is reserved for hostless contexts (model-driven ribbon/command scripts) or a deliberately separate deployable. Its title bar, expand and close button are platform chrome, light-only and not themeable (cite https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/developer/model-driven-apps/clientapi/reference/xrm-navigation/navigateto and https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/user/modern-fluent-design: dark mode not supported).
4. MUST: a page shown under platform chrome renders WizardShell embedded hideTitle (no double header). This codifies today's practice.
5. MUST NOT: inject CSS into or DOM-manipulate platform dialog chrome (cite https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/power-apps/developer/model-driven-apps/supported-customizations); a request to do so needs its own section 6.5 sign-off.
6. MUST: wizards default to dismiss="explicit" and pass uiScale like every other preset.
7. Unchanged: Layout 1 OOB entityrecord dialogs (85% x 85%), the fullCover escalation, and the MUST NOT on per-entity sizes.
8. RecordNavigationModalShell: record that it has zero live consumers; it is kept as the dirty-check protocol library behind onBeforeNavigate.
9. Companion doc fixes (not ADR text): MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md :33 (WizardShell is in @spaarke/ui-components; wizards point to MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md), :34 (yes/no confirms use ConfirmModal), :30 and :95-113 (Family 3 is BrowseModal + onBeforeNavigate), plus a new line "Launching from Spaarke React: in-app; from ribbon: navigateTo (white platform chrome)"; .claude/patterns/ui/record-modal-selection.md:26 and .claude/patterns/ui/modal-shell.md:16 (no longer "compose RecordNavigationModalShell"); docs/architecture/ui-dialog-shell-architecture.md (Three-Layer Model step 4 "embedded inside a Dataverse dialog" is the ribbon path only); ADR-026 matrix row cross-reference; MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md section 7 (WizardShell preset, WizardModal removed); .claude/CHANGELOG.md row.

Alternatives (for the ADR record): A (project exception) rejected because the conflict is general; C (comply) rejected because it means building on WizardModal, a second wizard engine. spec.md FR-60; D-26.
  </notes>

  <completion>DONE pending merge 2026-10-07 (main session): PR #1380 (branch docs/adr-050-wizard-amendment off master). Amendment points 1-8 applied to the concise ADR-050 (no full ADR-050 under docs/adr - recorded in the CHANGELOG entry); companion fixes (point 9) applied to MODAL-DECISION-CRITERIA.md, MODAL-DESIGN-SYSTEM.md section 7, record-modal-selection.md, modal-shell.md, ui-dialog-shell-architecture.md, ADR-026 matrix row; CHANGELOG entry names D-26 and task 110. All acceptance criteria verified by grep (preset list, retired WizardModal, MUSTs/MUST NOT, no legal-workspace / raw-Dialog confirm / compose-RecordNavigationModalShell instructions; Layout 1 + fullCover unchanged). Deviation: also fixed seven PRE-EXISTING broken relative links in the touched files (finding-triage rule: in-scope defect); link check 8 files / 0 broken. Mark completed when the owner merges #1380.</completion>

